"actor":"EO:14154","corroborated_by_two_jobs":false,"date":"2025-01-20","jobs":["later-events"]},"meta":{"acting_instrument_id":"EO:14154","date_basis":["acting order signing_date from OFR catalog","date stated next to the acting instrument in the OFR note"],"evidence_types":["ofr_note_on_acting","ofr_note_on_target"],"from":"later-events@jobs/later-events/output","from_job":"later-events","ids":["LE-1feac4575188","LE-3664730c8240"],"quote":"EO 14037, August 5, 2021","quote_kind":"verbatim_note_item","quote_truncated":false,"status":"CANDIDATE_UNVERIFIED"},"proposal":{"actor":"EO:14154","date":"2025-01-20","mechanism":"revocation","source":{"page_or_item":"OFR API record executive_order_number=14154; citation 90 FR 8353; document_number 2025-01956; field disposition_notes","sha256":"5523a353aca96f9b69e2d61bcf3528f15e9249d1a65ee2759a54fd7fe7d6d271","url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/documents?conditions%5Bcorrection%5D=0&conditions%5Bpresidential_document_type%5D=executive_order&conditions%5Btype%5D%5B%5D=PRESDOCU&fields%5B%5D=citation&fields%5B%5D=disposition_notes&fields%5B%5D=document_number&fields%5B%5D=executive_order_number&fields%5B%5D=html_url&fields%5B%5D=pdf_url&fields%5B%5D=president&fields%5B%5D=publication_date&fields%5B%5D=raw_text_url&fields%5B%5D=signing_date&fields%5B%5D=title&format=json&include_pre_1994_docs=true&order=executive_order_number&page=7&per_page=1000&search_after_cursor=WzEzNDk3LjAsIjEzNDk3Il0"}},"suggested":false}],"whole_order_end_total":3},"provisional_status":"no","readiness":{"by_step":{"clause_inventory":"confirm","counterevidence":"resolve_conflicts","ending_or_current_basis":"confirm","opus_media":"n/a","original_text":"confirm","savings_residuals":"agent_judgment","shared_sources":"n/a"},"needs_research":[],"would_satisfy_once_confirmed":["original_text","clause_inventory","ending_or_current_basis"]},"shared_sources":[],"signing_dates_seen":{"fr-originals@jobs/fr-originals/output":"2021-08-05","later-events_catalog":"2021-08-05","stage19_causal_queue":"2021-08-05","stage21_crosswalk":"2021-08-05"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:14037","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Section 1. Policy. America must lead the world on clean and efficient \ncars and trucks. That means bolstering our domestic market by setting a \ngoal that 50 percent of all new passenger cars and light trucks sold in \n2030 be zero-emission vehicles, including battery electric, plug-in hybrid \nelectric, or fuel cell electric vehicles. My Administration will prioritize \nsetting clear standards, expanding key infrastructure, spurring critical innova-\ntion, and investing in the American autoworker. This will allow us to \nboost jobs—with good pay and benefits—across the United States along \nthe full supply chain for the automotive sector, from parts and equipment \nmanufacturing to final assembly. \nIt is the policy of my Administration to advance these objectives in order \nto improve our economy and public health, boost energy security, secure \nconsumer savings, advance environmental justice, and address the climate \ncrisis.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 43583, PDF pages 1-3; Sec. 1","sha256":"3af2ef3f3e2f907f419720d3927f7b8e7c88b329208a94a4c08062f1603988fa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-08-10/pdf/2021-17121.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14037#sec1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. Light-, Medium-, and Certain Heavy-Duty Vehicles Multi-Pollutant \nand Fuel Economy Standards for 2027 and Later.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 43583, PDF pages 1-3; Sec. 2 (lead-in)","sha256":"3af2ef3f3e2f907f419720d3927f7b8e7c88b329208a94a4c08062f1603988fa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-08-10/pdf/2021-17121.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14037#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Administrator of the Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) shall, \nas appropriate and consistent with applicable law, consider beginning work \non a rulemaking under the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7401–7671q) to establish \nnew multi-pollutant emissions standards, including for greenhouse gas emis-\nsions, for light- and medium-duty vehicles beginning with model year 2027 \nand extending through and including at least model year 2030.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 43583, PDF pages 1-3; Sec. 2(a)","sha256":"3af2ef3f3e2f907f419720d3927f7b8e7c88b329208a94a4c08062f1603988fa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-08-10/pdf/2021-17121.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14037#sec2(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Secretary of Transportation shall, as appropriate and consistent \nwith applicable law, consider beginning work on a rulemaking under the \nEnergy Independence and Security Act of 2007 (Public Law 110–140, 121 \nStat. 1492) (EISA) to establish new fuel economy standards for passenger \ncars and light-duty trucks beginning with model year 2027 and extending \nthrough and including at least model year 2030.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 43583, PDF pages 1-3; Sec. 2(b)","sha256":"3af2ef3f3e2f907f419720d3927f7b8e7c88b329208a94a4c08062f1603988fa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-08-10/pdf/2021-17121.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14037#sec2(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) The Secretary of Transportation shall, as appropriate and consistent \nwith applicable law, consider beginning work on a rulemaking under EISA \nto establish new fuel efficiency standards for heavy-duty pickup trucks \nand vans beginning with model year 2028 and extending through and includ-\ning at least model year 2030.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 43583, PDF pages 1-3; Sec. 2(c)","sha256":"3af2ef3f3e2f907f419720d3927f7b8e7c88b329208a94a4c08062f1603988fa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-08-10/pdf/2021-17121.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14037#sec2(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 3. Heavy-Duty Engines and Vehicles Multi-Pollutant Standards for 2027 \nand Later.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 43583, PDF pages 1-3; Sec. 3 (lead-in)","sha256":"3af2ef3f3e2f907f419720d3927f7b8e7c88b329208a94a4c08062f1603988fa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-08-10/pdf/2021-17121.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14037#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Administrator of the EPA shall, as appropriate and con-\nsistent with applicable law, consider beginning work on a rulemaking under \nthe Clean Air Act to establish new oxides of nitrogen standards for heavy- \nduty engines and vehicles beginning with model year 2027 and extending \nthrough and including at least model year 2030.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 43583, PDF pages 1-3; Sec. 3(a)","sha256":"3af2ef3f3e2f907f419720d3927f7b8e7c88b329208a94a4c08062f1603988fa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-08-10/pdf/2021-17121.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14037#sec3(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Administrator of the EPA shall, as appropriate and consistent \nwith applicable law, and in consideration of the role that zero-emission \nheavy-duty vehicles might have in reducing emissions from certain market \nsegments, consider updating the existing greenhouse gas emissions standards \nVerDate Sep<11>2014 15:44 Aug 09, 2021 Jkt 253001 PO 00000 Frm 00001 Fmt 4705 Sfmt 4790 E:\\FR\\FM\\10AUE0.SGM 10AUE0jbell on DSKJLSW7X2PROD with EXECORD\n=== PDF page 2 of 3 ===\n43584 Federal Register / Vol. 86, No. 151 / Tuesday, August 10, 2021 / Presidential Documents \nfor heavy-duty engines and vehicles beginning with model year 2027 and \nextending through and including at least model year 2029.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 43583, PDF pages 1-3; Sec. 3(b)","sha256":"3af2ef3f3e2f907f419720d3927f7b8e7c88b329208a94a4c08062f1603988fa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-08-10/pdf/2021-17121.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14037#sec3(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 4. Medium- and Heavy-Duty Engines and Vehicles Greenhouse Gas \nand Fuel Efficiency Standards as Soon as 2030 and Later.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 43583, PDF pages 1-3; Sec. 4 (lead-in)","sha256":"3af2ef3f3e2f907f419720d3927f7b8e7c88b329208a94a4c08062f1603988fa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-08-10/pdf/2021-17121.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14037#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Adminis-\ntrator of the EPA shall, as appropriate and consistent with applicable law, \nconsider beginning work on a rulemaking under the Clean Air Act to establish \nnew greenhouse gas emissions standards for heavy-duty engines and vehicles \nto begin as soon as model year 2030.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 43583, PDF pages 1-3; Sec. 4(a)","sha256":"3af2ef3f3e2f907f419720d3927f7b8e7c88b329208a94a4c08062f1603988fa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-08-10/pdf/2021-17121.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14037#sec4(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Secretary of Transportation shall, as appropriate and consistent \nwith applicable law, consider beginning work on a rulemaking under EISA \nto establish new fuel efficiency standards for medium- and heavy-duty en-\ngines and vehicles to begin as soon as model year 2030.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 43583, PDF pages 1-3; Sec. 4(b)","sha256":"3af2ef3f3e2f907f419720d3927f7b8e7c88b329208a94a4c08062f1603988fa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-08-10/pdf/2021-17121.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14037#sec4(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) With respect to the rulemaking described \nin section 3(a) of this order, the Administrator of the EPA shall, as appropriate \nand consistent with applicable law, consider issuing a notice of proposed \nrulemaking by January 2022 and any final rulemaking by December 2022.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 43583, PDF pages 1-3; Sec. 5(a)","sha256":"3af2ef3f3e2f907f419720d3927f7b8e7c88b329208a94a4c08062f1603988fa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-08-10/pdf/2021-17121.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14037#sec5(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) With respect to the other rulemakings described in section 2 and \nsection 4 of this order, the Secretary of Transportation and the Administrator \nof the EPA shall, as appropriate and consistent with applicable law, consider \nissuing any final rulemakings no later than July 2024.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 43583, PDF pages 1-3; Sec. 5(b)","sha256":"3af2ef3f3e2f907f419720d3927f7b8e7c88b329208a94a4c08062f1603988fa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-08-10/pdf/2021-17121.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14037#sec5(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Secretary of Transportation \nand the Administrator of the EPA shall coordinate, as appropriate and con-\nsistent with applicable law, during the consideration of any rulemakings \npursuant to this order.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 43583, PDF pages 1-3; Sec. 6(a)","sha256":"3af2ef3f3e2f907f419720d3927f7b8e7c88b329208a94a4c08062f1603988fa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-08-10/pdf/2021-17121.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14037#sec6(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Secretary of Transportation and the Administrator of the EPA \nshall consult with the Secretaries of Commerce, Labor, and Energy on ways \nto achieve the goals laid out in section 1 of this order, to accelerate innovation \nand manufacturing in the automotive sector, to strengthen the domestic \nsupply chain for that sector, and to grow jobs that provide good pay and \nbenefits.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 43583, PDF pages 1-3; Sec. 6(b)","sha256":"3af2ef3f3e2f907f419720d3927f7b8e7c88b329208a94a4c08062f1603988fa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-08-10/pdf/2021-17121.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14037#sec6(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Given the significant expertise and historical leadership demonstrated \nby the State of California with respect to establishing emissions standards \nfor light-, medium-, and heavy-duty vehicles, the Administrator of the EPA \nshall coordinate the agency’s activities pursuant to sections 2 through 4 \nof this order, as appropriate and consistent with applicable law, with the \nState of California as well as other States that are leading the way in \nreducing vehicle emissions, including by adopting California’s standards.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 43583, PDF pages 1-3; Sec. 6(c)","sha256":"3af2ef3f3e2f907f419720d3927f7b8e7c88b329208a94a4c08062f1603988fa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-08-10/pdf/2021-17121.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14037#sec6(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d) In carrying out any of the actions described in this order, the Secretary \nof Transportation and the Administrator of the EPA shall seek input from \na diverse range of stakeholders, including representatives from labor unions, \nStates, industry, environmental justice organizations, and public health ex-\nperts.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 43583, PDF pages 1-3; Sec. 6(d)","sha256":"3af2ef3f3e2f907f419720d3927f7b8e7c88b329208a94a4c08062f1603988fa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-08-10/pdf/2021-17121.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14037#sec6(d)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Nothing in this order shall be construed \nto impair or otherwise affect: \n(i) the authority granted by law to an executive department or agency, \nor the head thereof; or \n(ii) the functions of the Director of the Office of Management and Budget \nrelating to budgetary, administrative, or legislative proposals.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"86 FR 43583, PDF pages 1-3; Sec. 7(a)","sha256":"3af2ef3f3e2f907f419720d3927f7b8e7c88b329208a94a4c08062f1603988fa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2021-08-10/pdf/2021-17121.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14037#sec7(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) This order shall be implemented consistent with applicable law and \nsubject to the availability of appropriations. \nVerDate Sep<11>2014 15:44 Aug 09, 2021 Jkt 253001 PO 00000 Frm 00002 Fmt 4705 Sfmt 4790 E:\\FR\\FM\\10AUE0.SGM 10AUE0jbell on DSKJLSW7X2PROD with EXECORD\n=== PDF page 3 of 3 ===\n43585 Federal Register / Vol. 86, No. 151 / Tuesday, August 10, 2021 / Presidential Documents \n(c) This order is not intended to, and does not, create any right or benefit, \nsubstantive or procedural, en